# DevPortfolio — Cursor rules

The canonical, complete guide for this repository is **[../AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md)**.
Read it before making changes. The essentials, so this file is useful on its own:

## The one rule
All **content** lives in `src/config.ts`. Edit that file for wording, projects,
awards, certifications, and the CV link. Only edit `src/components/*.astro` when you
need a new *kind* of section or a visual change.

## Project context
An Astro 5 + Tailwind CSS v4 static single-page portfolio, used for internship/job
interviews and scholarship applications. No database, no CMS, no tests.

## Hard invariants
1. Wrap local asset URLs in `withBase()` from `src/utils/url.ts` — GitHub Pages
   serves project repos from a sub-path. `http(s)://`, `mailto:`, `tel:` pass through.
2. Every section is guarded by `const hasX = siteConfig.x && siteConfig.x.length > 0;`
   so deleting a config array removes the section. Keep that pattern.
3. When adding a section, add its nav link to **both** `Header.astro` and
   `Footer.astro`, guarded the same way.
4. Use `siteConfig.accentColor` for themed elements. No second accent color.
5. Tailwind utility classes only; match the responsive breakpoints of neighbouring
   components (`sm:` `md:` `lg:` `xl:`).
6. Section layout convention: `<section id="…" class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">`
   → `grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start` with the heading
   in `lg:col-span-4` and content in `lg:col-span-8`.

## Commands
```bash
npm run dev      # dev server at http://localhost:4321
npm run build    # run before every push; must exit 0
npm run preview  # preview the production build
```

## Before you call a change done
`npm run build` exits 0, the new content appears in `dist/index.html`, and no
`— replace me` placeholder remains in the section you touched.
